    "text": "The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the system of linear equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;has infinitely many solutions, are respectively",
